#META 2026-11-24^November 20, 2026^May 2026 to October 2026 ¶ #NOTE 0~***Note: This calculation for the National Benefits Center’s processing time is specifically for adoption-based Form I-130s. The National Benefits Center adjudicates all adoption-based Form I-130s.***This processing time reflects statutory constraints on available immigrant visas, for which the wait times are typically much longer than the time it takes for USCIS to adjudicate the form.***USCIS service centers prioritize the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which an immigrant visa is available according to the Department of State Visa Bulletin. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing Form I-130 preference petitions. We are prioritizing our adjudication efforts to focus on cases that have visas available. ¶ #NOTE 1~***This processing time reflects statutory constraints on available immigrant visas, for which the wait times are typically much longer than the time it takes for USCIS to adjudicate the form.***USCIS service centers prioritize the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which an immigrant visa is available according to the Department of State Visa Bulletin. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing Form I-130 preference petitions. We are prioritizing our adjudication efforts to focus on cases that have visas available. ¶ #NOTE 2~***Note: This calculation for the National Benefits Center’s processing time is specifically for adoption-based Form I-130s. The National Benefits Center adjudicates all adoption-based Form I-130s.*** The Department of State visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. USCIS uses the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing a Form I-130 preference petition. ¶ #NOTE 3~USCIS service centers are now prioritizing the processing of Form I-130 preference petitions for which the Department of State Visa Bulletin shows that an immigrant visa is available. The visa bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. USCIS uses the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates before processing a Form I-130 preference petition. Service centers have prioritized our adjudication efforts so that we can focus on those cases that have visas available. ¶ #OFF NBC~National Benefits Center ¶ #OFF FOD~All Field Offices ¶ @I-130^134A-F21^Permanent resident filing for a spouse or child under 21|NBC:51.5:2022-05-07:0 FOD:36:2022-10-17:1 ¶ @I-130^134A-IR^U.S. citizen filing for a spouse, parent, or child under 21|NBC:51.5:2022-03-07:2 FOD:29.5:2023-02-14:3 ¶ @I-130^134B-F11^U.S. citizen filing for unmarried son/daughter 21 or older|NBC:50.5:2022-05-07:0 FOD:75:2018-11-08:1 ¶ @I-130^134B-F24^Permanent resident for unmarried son or daughter 21 or older|NBC:49.5:2022-05-16:0 FOD:61:2020-05-19:1 ¶ @I-130^134B-F31^U.S. citizen filing for a married son or daughter|NBC:62:2021-01-18:0 FOD:119:2014-04-18:1 ¶ @I-130^134B-F41^U.S. citizen filing for a brother or sister|NBC:66.5:2015-03-02:0 FOD:164:2012-03-06:1
